      <div type="clause" n="21">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 21</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De entercement de vif aveir, kil voldra clamer pur embled e voldrad duner gwage e truver plege a parsiure<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.1"/> sun apel, dunc estuvera<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.h"/> celui ki l’avera entre mains numer sun guarant, s’il l’ad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="xno" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.29"/><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De enter[cement<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="h" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.h-2"/>] de [vif<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.30"/>] aveir, kil voldrad clamer . . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.d"/> emblet e il volge doner wage e trover<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.31"/> plege a persiur[e]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.32"/> soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.17"/> apel, dunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.33"/> li stuverad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.34"/>, a celui qui l’auverad entre meins, nomer soun<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.17"/> guarant, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.35"/> il l’ad.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>De waranto producendo. Si clamauerit quis uiuum auerium quasi furto sibi surreptum et dederit uadium et inuenerit plegios de clamio prosequendo, oportet eum qui rem in manu habet warantum suum producere.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="21" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="264" ed="#robertson"/>De entercement de vif aveir: kil voldra clamer pur embled e voldrad duner gwage e truver plege a parsivre sun apel, dunc estuvera celui ki l'avera entre mains numer sun guarant s'il l'ad.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="506–507" ed="#liebermann"/>21. Betreffend Anefang<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#missing"/> von Lebgut: wer [= wenn jemand] es als [ihm] gestohlen beanspruchen will und für die Verfolgung seiner Klage Pfand geben und Bürgschaft finden will, dann muss der [Besitzer], der es in Händen hat, seinen Gewährsmann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.de.4"/> nennen, wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#LeisWl_21.lnote.de.5"/> er solchen hat.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">21. Concerning the attachment of live goods: whoever [= if someone] wishes to claim it as stolen [from him] and wishes to give pledge and find surety for the prosecution of his suit, then the [possessor] who has it in his hands must name his warrantor, if he has such.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="265" ed="#robertson"/>The attachment of livestock: if anyone desires to claim it as stolen, and is willing to give pledge and find surety for prosecuting his claim, he who has possession of it must name his warrantor, if he has one.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="409"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:WlArt_5">Wl art 5</ref> <quote>cf. also Leis Wl 21 – 21:5, Wl art. 5 on witnessing and attachment of livestock</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 264–265 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 506–507, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.h" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">ergänzt MAT. aus I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a supplied by MAT. from I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">parsuire <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">parsuire Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze aus HkL</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply from HkL</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.h-2" n="h" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">enierz <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> eiuers <hi rend="italic">Io abgekürzt?</hi> entremeins <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> e. de vif <hi rend="italic">Wilkins</hi> (<hi rend="italic">nach Somner’s Erfindung?</hi>)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">enierz Im; eiuers Io abbreviated? entremeins instead of e. de vif Wilkins (following an invention of Somner’s?)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">son <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XXV. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XXV. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">jus <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> ins <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">jus Im; ins Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">trouuer <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">trouuer Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">persuir <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">persuir I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dunt <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dunt Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scuv. <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scuv. Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">506</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sul <hi rend="italic">statt</hi> si il <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sul instead of si il Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.de.1_3" n="1—3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anefang 1c. 4A. 5. 12; Prozessualpfand 8A; <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 45, 1{1}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anefang 1c. 4A. 5. 12; Prozessualpfand 8A; <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 45, 1{1}</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies gilt für Mercien, dagegen für Wessex und Denalagu (21, 3; 4) anderes Recht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This applies to Mercia, whereas Wessex and the Denalagu (21, 3; 4) have different law</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_21.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">289</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zwei solche überflüssigen Bedingungssätze <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 21, 1{3}; 1a{3}. L lässt dies fort</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Two such superfluous conditional clauses <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 21, 1{3}; 1a{3}. L omits this</seg></note>
      </div>
